  "methodology": "Political-hotbed is a sourced selection of campuses with documented, consequential political speech or protest activity. This 25-campus candidate set combines 23 campuses explicitly discussed in The Chronicle's 2024 report on student encampments, plus Georgetown University and Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute, which FIRE identifies among schools repeatedly performing poorly in its multi-year political-speech controversy rankings. The Chronicle cohort is concentrated on one 2024 issue and is not a balanced measure of ideology or a claim that these campuses have higher activism than unlisted campuses. FIRE's survey measures speech climate and political tolerance, not activism frequency. Revisit as more cross-ideological event data is sourced.",
